From 51009ff4b3904994bdede8d7ee280d6ca6249605 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:31:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 218/225] feat: rebuild the hit material in ShadePS, not in the
 tracer (decision 11)

The trace pass wrote a fully decoded material and that did not fit fxc: ConeTracePS plus one
BVH walk plus RT_ProcessBestHit answered "internal error: compilation aborted unexpectedly"
on the engine's real specular permutation, and d8f5dad4 bought the room by gating the blend
layer out. The two jobs are now in two shaders and the gate is gone.

TRACE PASS (ConeTracePS) keeps the search and nothing else: the BVH walk, the alpha / stipple
acceptance test with its one albedo atlas tap, the nearest hit, and the voxel irradiance + AO
at the hit (it needs the brick pools). Its answer is a new HITID target on SV_Target5, RGBA32F,
replacing HITMAT:

  .x = triangle record index + 1        0 = miss / never written
  .y = material record index + 1
  .z = round(u * 65535)                 barycentric u, 16 bit
  .w = round(v * 65535) * 16 + flags    barycentric v, 16 bit, plus back-face / sprite /
                                        stipple-phase bits

Four exact float integers, not asuint bit patterns: ETEX_Format has no integer render target,
and asfloat(5) is a denormal the output merger may flush to zero. Everything is inside fp32's
exact-integer range; the ceiling is 16.7 M records.

SHADE PASS (ShadePS) gains RT_ReconstructHit, which is stage 5B's reconstruction moved whole:
tangent frame, raw uv, base + extras + blend records, every atlas sample, detail map, BLEND
LAYER (ungated - decision 10's feature is back), per type parameters, F0, smoothness, emissive.
ALD / RGB no longer carry albedo or normal for RT pixels; they keep the voxel cone colour, which
makes them the right fallback if the shade pass does not run. RGB.w is still the reflecting
pixel's depth for DemosaicPS. HITPOS.w is free (it held RT_PackHitMaterial). The emissive hue is
now an fp32 float3 instead of a 3-bit-per-channel PackRGB code in ALD.w, and F0 no longer goes
through the 2D square-law quantisation at all.

The voxel AO probe walks along the winning triangle's GEOMETRIC face normal (SBestHit.faceNorm,
now filled unconditionally and oriented against the ray). The shading normal does not exist in
that pass any more, and the geometric one is the better input for a probe that measures solid
neighbours in front of the surface.

Debug views 2, 3, 10, 11 and 12 move to ShadePS with the quantities they show; 1, 4 and 5 stay
in the tracer, where the search is. View 6 now shows the raw albedo texel (the material tint and
the detail / blend deltas are ShadePS' now).

REGISTERS: geomPool_TTex moves from t28 to t55. ShadePS reads both pools now and t28 is
ForwardShading.cfi's Fwd_ShadowMap2 on that technique. t9 (geomPool_Tris) was already free
there. ShadePass binds both pools, ssSvoLinearClamp at s1, and uploads SVO_RTPoolInfo and
SVO_RTParams1; the brick-pool prohibition at t0-t3 is unchanged.

FXC: RT_RecordTC((int)vEx1.x) written inline at the blend layer's call site CRASHES fxc, with
no line number, on both compiler builds, at every -O level, on ps_5_0 and ps_5_1. Reduced to a
490 line standalone file with no CRYENGINE include in it: assigning the same value to a named
local first makes it compile. It is the optimiser's stack, not a size limit - the integer
divides inside RT_RecordTC are innocent and deleting blocks elsewhere does not move it. Every
RT_RecordTC argument in the reconstruction now goes through its own local, and the rule is
written at the call site.

Validation: rtharness2 33 ok / 0 FAIL with both the SDK fxc 10.0.26100.7705 and the engine's
d3dcompiler_47.dll 10.0.26100.9444, with the blend layer LIVE. Trace pass listing 3297 -> 2976
lines, shade pass 1852 -> 2243 (and the shade figure now contains a blend layer the baseline had
nowhere). Headroom measured by adding four synthetic extra material layers to ShadePS: still
compiles. cryfx_lint.py clean on all four shader files. CryRenderD3D11 Profile 0 errors,
0 warnings. Native path unchanged: every shader hunk is inside an existing %_RT_ block or in a
function unreferenced off-flag, and every C++ hunk is inside an e_svoTI_RT_Active guard.

GAP: a sprite (particle) hit cannot be reconstructed from a triangle record and a pair of
barycentrics - its uv comes from a billboard tile table and its albedo is blended over several
taps. RT_HITID_FLAG_SPRITE marks one and the ordinary triangle path is taken. Nothing produces
sprite hits today; stage 4 has to revisit it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SCUvWGLCsqzm3VNMzp4uiS
